From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Masta2002 <Masta2002@gmx.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:44:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] fftools/ffmpeg: stream specifiers can select streams by
 codec

The stream type in a stream specifier of the ffmpeg tool may be followed
by a codec name:

    stream_type[:codec_name][:additional_stream_specifier]

    ffmpeg -i IN -map 0 -c copy -c:a:aac libopus OUT

encodes the AAC audio streams with libopus and copies everything else.
a:aac:1 is the second AAC audio stream. For output streams mapped from an
input stream the codec name refers to the input codec, also when the
stream is reencoded. Output streams fed by a complex filtergraph have no
input codec and are never matched by a codec name.

Existing specifier forms keep their meaning: the token after the stream
type is only taken as a codec name when it is the name of a codec
descriptor of that media type. Tokens starting with a digit (index),
single letters (stream types, p, g, i, m, u) and disp are never looked up,
so a:1, a:#0x100, a:i:256, a:m:language:eng, v:disp:default, a:p:1 parse
exactly as before, and a:h264 is rejected as before.

Based on skyjet18/FFmpeg release/6.1-patched d7c69e96ce
("avformat: added support for stream codec specifier type in -c argument").

Port: in 6.1 the ffmpeg options were matched with libavformat's
avformat_match_stream_specifier(), so the feature was added to the library.
In 9.0.2 ffmpeg parses specifiers itself with stream_specifier_parse() /
stream_specifier_match() in fftools/cmdutils.c, so the codec is parsed
into StreamSpecifier.codec_id and matched there instead; this also covers
-map, filtergraph input labels and per-stream AVOptions. The public
library function is left unchanged, and so are ffprobe -select_streams and
ffplay -ast/-vst/-sst, which use it: they do not know the codec form.

As in the original, ost_add() stores the input codec id in the output
AVStream while the output options are evaluated. Nothing reads the codec
id of an output stream before of_stream_init() replaces the whole codecpar
with the streamcopy/encoder/bsf parameters (avcodec_parameters_copy() in
bsf_init()), and the header is only written once every stream of the file
went through of_stream_init(), so the value never reaches the muxer or the
output of a reencoded stream.

Unlike the original, a codec name of another media type or a codec name
starting with a digit is not consumed, and the library test is replaced by
FATE tests of the ffmpeg tool which need no external samples.
