diff --git a/doc/ffmpeg.texi b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
index 882503142e..22a615c859 100644
--- a/doc/ffmpeg.texi
+++ b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
@@ -822,6 +822,15 @@ ffmpeg -i INPUT -map 0 -c copy -c:v:1 libx264 -c:a:137 libvorbis OUTPUT
 will copy all the streams except the second video, which will be encoded with
 libx264, and the 138th audio, which will be encoded with libvorbis.
 
+A stream specifier may also select mapped streams by their input codec. For
+example
+@example
+ffmpeg -i INPUT -map 0 -c copy -c:a:aac libopus OUTPUT
+@end example
+will encode AAC audio streams with libopus and copy all other streams. The
+codec name is part of the stream specifier appended to @code{-c}; it is not the
+@var{codec} argument. See the @ref{Stream specifiers} chapter.
+
 @item -t @var{duration} (@emph{input/output})
 When used as an input option (before @code{-i}), limit the @var{duration} of
 data read from the input file.
